    :hasEvidenceText "Comparison between Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) and Chain-of-Experts (CoE)."^^xsd:string,
        "Given the autoregressive nature of Mixture of Experts (MoE) computations, it is vital to maintain consistency across time steps"^^xsd:string,
        "Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) based sparsely activated neural networks have been introduced for training larger models"^^xsd:string,
        "MoE Jetpack converts pre-trained dense models into MoE models, enhancing convergence and performance"^^xsd:string,
        "MoE differs from dense models by using multiple specialized sub-networks, where each input activates only a subset of experts"^^xsd:string,
        "MoE model inference at scale"^^xsd:string,
        "MoE models differ in the number of active parametersMoE uses just a fraction of them."^^xsd:string,
        "Model SRP MoE A:T S:A"^^xsd:string,
        "Since the experts are distributed across different devices, communication during this process i"^^xsd:string,
        "The MoE models dense counterparts are selected to be FLOP-equivalent"^^xsd:string,
        "The sparse Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) layer [ 58 ], consists of multiple feed-forward networks (FFNs), termed experts, and a trainable"^^xsd:string,
        "The sparsely activated mixture of experts (MoE) model presents a promising alternative to traditional densely activated (dense) models"^^xsd:string,
        "distributing input samples to these scattered experts demands resource-intensive all-to-all communication (Fig. 1 ). High communication volume in all-to-all operations significantly hampers the training speed of MoE models"^^xsd:string,
        "expert parameters account for the majority of MoE-based LLMs model size (see Figure 3) and only a small fraction of experts are activated during inference"^^xsd:string,
        "four MoE models: Mixtral-8 7B [16] and Switch-32/64/128 with 32, 64, and 128 experts per layer"^^xsd:string,
        "integrate multiple smaller sub-models or experts within a comprehensive ensemble model."^^xsd:string,
        "parallel FFNs called experts. In each MoE layer, a trainable gate network routes each token to only the top- experts."^^xsd:string,
        "parallel FFNs called experts. In each MoE layer, a trainable gate network routes each token to only the top- experts. As experts are sparsely activated, MoE enables scaling model parameters"^^xsd:string,
        "the dense and MoE models use 7.02GB and 21.16GB, respectively"^^xsd:string,
        "the quality of the MoE model can be continuously improved by increasing the capacity factor"^^xsd:string,
        "within MoE models, thus enhancing efficiency."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :model,
        owl:Thing ;
    owl:disjointWith :dense_model ;
    skos:altLabel "MoE model"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A sparsely activated neural network architecture that uses multiple specialized sub-networks where each input activates only a subset of parameters."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom "CQ_S0_R1_0010"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0013"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0014"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0038"^^xsd:string,
