    kg:textSpan "models are constrained by training time, MoE models scale better due to their sublinear computing cost increase. A dense model with 1 trillion parameters requires 3 months to train on 3072 NVIDIA A100 GPUs, but an MoE model can be trained in weeks [14]. However, the models scalability depends on device memory capacity. The differences in I/O latency between HBM in GPUs, CPU memory, and SSDs cause delays, necessitating efficient storage management for sparsely activated training [32]. Our Contrib" .

