    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2410_17954v1_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "tokens distribution across experts is typically uneven, causing some experts to handle very few tokens. According to the roofline model [ 43 ], the computational cost of processing a single token is nearly equivalent to that of multiple tokens. This imbalance results in underutilization of computational resources, as many experts are not fully leveraged. These dual-dimensional inefficiencies underscore the inherent challenges in optimizing MoE systems for efficient inference. Opportunity 3: Cost" .

