    kg:textSpan "generation lengths of 64 or more. With 210GB of KV cache and a generation length of 64, decode and prefill throughput curves are noticeably smoother, reflecting fewer sequence preemptions due to ample cache capacity. This leads to higher overall throughput and better GPU utilization. A similar trend is observed for generation lengths of 128 and 256. Preemptions, if any, occur only in the early stages of execution, and the throughput stabilizes quickly. In the 256-token case, the duration of pref" .

