    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2504_12463_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "forward passes through experts. Equation ( 4 ) describes the dense gradient of the router for an individual token. Each expert output E i ( x ) in the router gradient corresponds to updating the embedding for expert i in the routing layer (i.e. the i th row of the router parameters W ). In a standard sparse MoE, the gradient only includes expert outputs E i for the experts i A selected by the Top-K routing function. The other terms are essentially 0 , which means that non-activated experts can n" .

