    kg:textSpan "devices, allowing for parallel processing of tensors within layers[ 31 ]. TP can significantly reduce the memory consumption of each model rank but introduces some intra-layer communication overhead. DP distributes batches of data across replicas of the model on different devices, aggregating gradients during training[ 35 ]. Zero Redundancy Optimizer(ZeRO) further splits optimizer states, model weights and gradients across DP group to trade memory with communication [ 16 ; 27 ]. CP splits the in" .

