    kg:textSpan "Manipulation As discussed in Section 2.1 , current systems impose a fixed capacity limit on the number of tokens that can be routed to each expert class. Expert capacity aims to avoid long iterations and idle resources due to the high variance in expert popularity. However, this causes dropped tokens, which harms training convergence. Expert capacity in current systems is defined as: capacity ( e i ) = capacity_factor tokens_per_batch E ( 1 ) == capacity_factor tokens_per_batch r sN | {z } slot_" .

