    kg:textSpan "key assumptions. First, increasing the frequency of adaptive replication directly translates to fewer dropped tokens. In total, S YMI dropped 69% , 64% , 62% and 43% fewer tokens over the course of training compared to DeepSpeed, FlexMoE-100, FlexMoE-50, and FlexMoE-10, respectively. Secondly, combined with the 5.2 Convergence Evaluation Figure 7 shows the training loss of all systems over the course of 2,000 training iterations. S YMI achieves significantly faster convergence than DeepSpeed thr" .

