    kg:textSpan "experts dominate and safety-preferring components are effectively muted. Importantly, our results indicate that the router implicitly treats safety as its own task, allocating it a sparse subnetwork of experts; unlike other domains where sparsity is beneficial, this separation is undesirable because small routing shifts can marginalize the safety pathway altogether. The unique risks introduced by expert routing underscore the need for stronger alignment strategies tailored to MoE LLMs, as well a" .

