    kg:textSpan "experts in each layer using activation frequency heuristics, whereas search based methods such as EEP [ 27 ] and NAEE [ 30 ] enumerate all k expert combinations inside each MoE layer. Unfortunately, considering the discrepancy of expert redundancy across different MoE layers (i.e., more number of experts are required to be activated in shadow layers than deeper layers, as demonstrated in Sec. 5.3.2), simply applying uniform pruning ratio for all layers may cause poor performance during inference" .

