    kg:textSpan "involves converting a pre-trained dense model into an MoE by replicating its feed-forward network (FFN) layers to form multiple, initially identical experts. While this provides a strong initialization, it suffers from a knowledge bottleneck and a lack of initial expert diversity, as all experts originate from a single source. To address this, Drop-Upcycling (Nakamura et al. 2025) performs partial re-initialization to enhance expert diversity. Branch-Train-Mix strategy (Sukhbaatar et al. 2024; H" .

