    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2510_13079_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "conceptualize this as analyzing how expert specializations propagate through their gating patterns. Experts with similar gating weight vectors tend to be activated by similar types of tokens, indicating that their learned specializations have propagated along similar directions in the parameter space, potentially leading to functional overlap. We define the cosine similarity matrix of the gating weights S R n n as: S ij := w g,i , w g,j | w g,i | | w g,j | (5) where w g,i and w g,j are the i -th" .

