    kg:textSpan "be affected by batch size. 2) Partitioning introduces more smaller operators, thereby incurring GPU kernel launching overhead and under-utilization of streaming multiprocessors. Overpartitioning computations can lead to excessive overhead, negating the benefits of overlapping. Conversely, insufficient partitioning hinders the full utilization of potential overlap with all-to-all communication. Additionally, gating methods limit the types of operators that can be partitioned. Hence, extending the" .

