    kg:textSpan "we define a fair comparison of an MoE model against its dense counterpart by aligning for both, the same number of active parameters (i.e. FLOP aligned, short: FA ) and total parameters (i.e. parameter aligned, short: PA ). We further assume that a fair comparison between models should reduce confounding factors. Along those lines, we normalize models for training datasets, recipes, and architectures wherever possible. This way, we can make a clear performance attribution to the MoE component in" .

