    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2504_14960_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "by increasing the sequence length while keeping the total number of tokens per global batch constant. As shown in Figure 4, our framework can train MoE models with high efficiency up to a context length of 128K tokens, and the MFU only drops from 38.7% to 35.9% for Qwen-57B14A and 47.6% to 42.9% for Mixtral-8x22B. With MoE parallel folding, MCore can achieve higher performance by folding the parallelism groups of attention and MoE layers to better utilize the intra-node communication bandwidth. " .

