    kg:textSpan "layers and the number of experts per layer as m and n , respectively. Although advanced MoE offloading proposes compressing experts using ultralow-bit quantization (e.g., INT2 , INT1 ) to reduce transfer costs, this significantly degrades model performance. As mentioned in the introduction, expert offloading shifts the decoding bottleneck from memory-bound to I/O bound. Specifically, the expert transferring from DRAM to VRAM incurs long latency. For example, the expert in the Mixtral- 8 7B model" .

