    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2505_08944_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "the layers own -queue. Due to adaptive rebatching, GPUs do not need to wait for barrier-style all-to-all communication to finish. Instead, they stay busy as long as enough load is offered at any layer. By colocating more than one expert layer on a GPU, scheduler can multiplex layers to prioritize execution of hot experts with enough input tokens and let cold experts to accumulate more tokens before execution. To demonstrate the efficacy of AEP, we built a prototype MoE serving, AMoE. With a smal" .

