    :hasEvidenceText "In transformer-based large language models (LLMs), each mixture-of-experts (MoE) layer typically consists of a set of N expert networks"^^xsd:string,
        "MegaScale-MoE reduces the communication volume by customizing parallelism strategies for the attention and FFN modules in each MoE layer."^^xsd:string,
        "Since MoE layer weights 1 Introduction Mixture of Experts (MoE) models have emerged as a powerful paradigm"^^xsd:string,
        "The Mixture of Experts (MoE) is an effective architecture for scaling large language models by leveraging sparse expert activation"^^xsd:string,
        "The MoE layer replaces the standard FFN with a mixture of experts, allowing the model to dynamically select a subset of experts for each input token."^^xsd:string,
        "We can derive the load balancing score by calculating the mean of scores across all l MoE layers"^^xsd:string,
        "each mixture-of-experts (MoE) layer typically consists of a set of N expert networks"^^xsd:string,
        "replacing every other Transformer blocks feed-forward layer with an MoE layer"^^xsd:string,
        "when distributing MoE layers, each device holds a subset of experts along with all other non-expert parameters"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:skos_definition "A layer in transformer-based large language models that replaces the traditional feed-forward network with a set of expert networks and a gating mechanism."^^xsd:string ;
