    :hasEvidenceText "As the size of an MoE model is dominated by the weights of the experts"^^xsd:string,
        "For MT, the dense and MoE models use 7.02GB and 21.16GB, respectively"^^xsd:string,
        "Mixture of Expert (MoE) enables a nearly constant computational budget as model scaling. Generally, we replace some layers of a foundation model with MoE ones to generate a MoE model."^^xsd:string,
        "Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architectures for efficient scaling"^^xsd:string,
        "Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) based sparsely activated neural networks have been introduced for training larger models with minimal or no additional computational resources"^^xsd:string,
        "MoE Models: Our models consist of two stacked LSTM layers with a MoE layer between them"^^xsd:string,
        "MoE models can be easily scaled to attain enhanced model performance by adding more experts"^^xsd:string,
        "MoE models contain several sequential MoE blocks [ 59 , 97 ]. As shown in Figure 1a, each MoE block has an attention layer, a gate unit, and several parallel feed-forward networks (FFNs) called experts ."^^xsd:string,
        "MoE models, achieving an order-of-magnitude reduction in training cost compared to dense models with equivalent model quality."^^xsd:string,
        "Sparsely-Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) layer, which laid the foundation for scaling neural networks by utilizing a sparse activation pattern."^^xsd:string,
        "The Mixtures-of-Experts (MoE) model is a widespread distributed and integrated learning method for large language models (LLM)"^^xsd:string,
        "The experts within a sparsely activated MoE mo"^^xsd:string,
        "Their goal was to decouple the model parameters from the computational cost of trainin"^^xsd:string,
        "expert routing data from the OpenMoE and Mixtral models"^^xsd:string,
        "for a fixed model size M and activation ratio A , we vary the expert granularity"^^xsd:string,
        "the quality of the MoE model can be continuously improved by increasing the capacity factor"^^xsd:string,
        "tokens are only routed to partial experts for computation. Figure 2 shows the typical execution flow of an MoE layer and Table 1 explains symbols to describe the execution of an MoE model."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :model,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:skos_definition "A model architecture consisting of experts and a gating function, often used to increase capacity without proportional increases in computational cost."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom "CQ_S0_R1_0066"^^xsd:string,
