    kg:textSpan "10 summarizes the effect of different gating policies on memory consumption, using single node cases as an example. Dynamic gating enables larger batch sizes, which runs even faster, when compared against the static gating policy with smaller batch sizes. Dynamic gating reduces the memory footprint by removing the dispatch mask, and also reduces wasted memory allocations for empty paddings and placeholders. As a result, the memory allocated for the activation (bright colors in the figure) for LM" .

