    kg:textSpan "256 [ 1 , 16 ]. Rather than propagating tokens to all experts, MoE models dynamically route each token to only a subset of experts. Since a single model generally cannot fit all experts within the memory of a single GPU , parts of the model are processed by different GPU s. To address this, MoE model inference typically relies on expert parallelism ( EP ). With EP , the self-attention and router layers are replicated across GPUs, while the experts are distributed across GPUs [ 1 ]. During the fo" .

