    kg:docId "2404.15159_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2404_15159_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan ") = where W is the pretrained weights of the FFN layer, which is shared by { E k } K k =1 , R ( ) denotes the Top-K router we employed to select specific LoRA experts for different tokens and tasks and E k ( ) represents k -th LoRA experts in the M IX L O RA module. The role of M IX L O RA is to replace the FFN layer of the dense models in Equation 5, and its key concept is to select different experts by the router for each token, where each expert is composed of a different LoRA and origin FFN " .

