    :hasEvidenceText "Compared to Expert Drop, both Layer Drop and Block Drop focus on structures beyond expert level"^^xsd:string,
        "Each input token is assigned to one or more experts for computation"^^xsd:string,
        "Even modest batch sizes (8-16) cause all experts to be activated"^^xsd:string,
        "Exp. represents individual experts"^^xsd:string,
        "Fiddler puts a subset of expert layers into the GPU memory."^^xsd:string,
        "Figures 5a , 5b , and 5c compare the perplexity achieved by our method and the dense baseline on the routed dataset segments for the 1 . 3 B parameter model, utilizing mixtures of 4 , 16 , and 32 experts"^^xsd:string,
        "Grouping high-affinity experts on the same device"^^xsd:string,
        "MoE models activate only specific experts per token, unlike dense models that utilize the entire model for every token."^^xsd:string,
        "MoE with 4 or 8 experts shows the best quality (lowest validation loss) under a certain inference cost."^^xsd:string,
        "MoEs learn to route inputs to a sparse set of their feedforward parameters."^^xsd:string,
        "N i represents the number of tokens assigned to the i -th expert"^^xsd:string,
        "Parameters corresponding to each partition is referred to as an expert"^^xsd:string,
        "Parameters corresponding to each partition is referred to as an expert, and this architecture is known as the Sparse M"^^xsd:string,
        "Switch Transformer [6] with 256 experts per block requires more than 50GB memory"^^xsd:string,
        "The tokens in are then processed by the appropriate experts"^^xsd:string,
        "Typically, each expert in the MoE layer is a compact neural network consisting of several feed-forward layers followed by an activation function"^^xsd:string,
        "We move the expert parameters to CPU memory to reduce burden on GPU memory."^^xsd:string,
        "activating only a subset of parameters (experts) for each input."^^xsd:string,
        "allowing each expert to learn independently as a separate neural network"^^xsd:string,
        "assigning a gating score for each expert using a trainable linear layer"^^xsd:string,
        "consists of N experts, each instantiated as an independent FFN."^^xsd:string,
        "distributes the input data to the selected experts"^^xsd:string,
        "distributing tokens evenly across experts maximizes computational efficiency"^^xsd:string,
        "each FP16 expert contains approximately 4 , 096 14 , 336 2 2 bytes of weight data."^^xsd:string,
        "each GPU accommodates more than one expert during inference"^^xsd:string,
        "each expert is composed of a different LoRA and origin FFN layer"^^xsd:string,
        "each expert receives 1 /N fraction of tokens"^^xsd:string,
        "expert models that provide diverse but complementary insights into the data distribution"^^xsd:string,
        "experts are distributed across different devices"^^xsd:string,
        "identify the most M relevant experts for the unlearning task"^^xsd:string,
        "if a token activates an expert not cached in fast memory"^^xsd:string,
        "incorporating multiple expert networks and employing a sparse gating mechanism"^^xsd:string,
        "integrate multiple smaller sub-models or experts within a comprehensive ensemble model."^^xsd:string,
        "intermediate hidden dimension in the expert FFN layers"^^xsd:string,
        "layer-wise routers select the l -th layer expert"^^xsd:string,
        "layer-wise routers select the l -th layer expert i"^^xsd:string,
        "necessitating uniform input batch sizes across all experts"^^xsd:string,
        "parallel FFNs called experts."^^xsd:string,
        "parallel FFNs called experts. In each MoE layer, a trainable gate network routes each token to only the top- experts."^^xsd:string,
        "resulting in a consistent pattern of token processing by the same experts throughout training"^^xsd:string,
        "route each input token to a subset of experts for computation"^^xsd:string,
        "route each token to a top- k subset of experts"^^xsd:string,
        "the expert is usually contr"^^xsd:string,
        "the expert with the highest gating weight for each token is selected to process the input"^^xsd:string,
        "the experts are distributed across GPUs"^^xsd:string,
        "the most burdened experts dictate the overall latency of the MoE layer"^^xsd:string,
        "the number of dropped tokens for the i -th expert"^^xsd:string,
        "the router does not receive a gradient update from experts that it does not activate"^^xsd:string,
        "tokens are only routed to partial experts for computation."^^xsd:string,
        "we denote the i th expert on layer j as E i,j"^^xsd:string,
        "we solely optimize the router to preserve the explicit semantic distinction of expert modules."^^xsd:string,
        "when the load exceeds the capacity, experts must discard excess tokens to adhere to the constraint."^^xsd:string ;
